<title>HUNGARY: NEW AUTO SALES IN CENTRAL EUROPE -- MARCH TABLE.</title>
<headline>NEW AUTO SALES IN CENTRAL EUROPE -- MARCH TABLE.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>New auto sales in Central</p>
<p>European Free Trade Agreement (CEFTA) countries rose 25.4</p>
<p>percent to 86,884 units in March 1997 from 69,311 units in</p>
<p>March 1996, according to a monthly Reuters survey.</p>
<p>CEFTA, which was formed in 1993, includes the Czech</p>
<p>Republic, Hungary, Poland, Slovakia and Slovenia. The survey</p>
<p>covers cars, minibuses, pickups, vans and other four-wheeled</p>
<p>motor vehicles not over five tonnes in gross weight.</p>
